  {
   "file": "fig_order",
   "width": "full",
   "caption": "Energy-error order test on the production system (N = 1000, η = 0.35, 20+/20−, l_B = 5 σ): maximum |E(t) − E(0)|/N over 2 τ of NVE dynamics versus the step h for the four integrators, with the fitted log–log slopes in the legends and dashed reference lines ∝ h and ∝ h². (a) Equilibrated start (15 τ with charges on): the shipped cv-phys is second order (slope 2.02) whereas the literal HLL collision Verlet is only first order (slope 0.73) and 35× less accurate at the production step h = 0.005 τ; kdk-phys gives 1.81 and the naive splitting 1.09. (b) Same test from the un-equilibrated start with Ewald (solid; slopes 1.40 / 0.78 / 1.69 / 0.89) and with the smooth DSF Coulomb model (dashed, cv-phys 1.92, cv 1.21); the Ewald real-space truncation erfc(αr_c) ≈ 7.5×10⁻⁵ sets a floor of ≈ 10⁻⁶ kT/N at h = 0.0025 τ that flattens every Ewald curve there.",
